    "created_at": "2022-03-02T07:02:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-02T07:02:45Z",
    "body": "> I dug up #34 which contains a bunch of arguments against trailer support. I'm not sure if those are still current, as it's been a while.\r\n\r\nI read the thread. The arguments against mostly don't apply to `Server-Timing`. A lot of the argument are against exposing the trailers in `fetch()` / `XHR`, and that in many other standard header cases trailers would be nonsensical or harmful.\r\n\r\nHowever timing info was presented there as an actual valid specific use case.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
